<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
<title>Gulp of Knowledge — Culinary Trivia</title>
<link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Playfair+Display:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;0,900;1,400;1,700&family=Libre+Baskerville:ital,wght@0,400;0,700;1,400&family=DM+Sans:wght@300;400;500&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">
<style>
  :root {
    --cream: #F7F3EC;
    --ink: #1A1410;
    --rust: #C4522A;
    --gold: #B8963E;
    --sage: #5C6B4E;
    --warm-gray: #8B7D6B;
    --light-rule: #DDD4C4;
    --white: #FDFAF6;
  }

  * { margin: 0; padding: 0; box-sizing: border-box; }

  body {
    background: var(--cream);
    color: var(--ink);
    font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif;
    min-height: 100vh;
    overflow-x: hidden;
  }

  /* ── MASTHEAD ── */
  .masthead {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--cream);
    text-align: center;
    padding: 18px 24px 14px;
    border-bottom: 3px solid var(--rust);
    position: relative;
  }
  .masthead-kicker {
    font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif;
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .masthead-title {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: clamp(38px, 8vw, 72px);
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 1;
    letter-spacing: -0.02em;
  }
  .masthead-title span { color: var(--rust); font-style: italic; }
  .masthead-sub {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-size: 13px;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    margin-top: 6px;
    letter-spacing: 0.02em;
  }
  .masthead-rule {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 12px;
    margin-top: 12px;
  }
  .masthead-rule span { width: 60px; height: 1px; background: var(--warm-gray); }
  .masthead-rule em { font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif; font-size: 16px; color: var(--gold); }

  /* ── LAYOUT ── */
  .page { max-width: 900px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 0 20px 60px; }

  /* ── CHAPTER GRID (home) ── */
  #screen-home { animation: fadeIn 0.4s ease; }

  .section-label {
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
    padding-top: 10px;
    margin: 32px 0 20px;
  }

  .intro-block {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0;
    border: 1px solid var(--light-rule);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--ink);
    margin: 28px 0 0;
    background: var(--white);
  }
  .intro-text {
    padding: 28px 28px 28px 28px;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--light-rule);
  }
  .intro-text h2 {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: 28px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .intro-text h2 em { color: var(--rust); }
  .intro-text p {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #4A3F35;
  }
  .intro-stats {
    padding: 28px;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 20px;
  }
  .stat {
    text-align: center;
    padding-bottom: 20px;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--light-rule);
  }
  .stat:last-child { border-bottom: none; padding-bottom: 0; }
  .stat-num {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: 42px;
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--rust);
    line-height: 1;
  }
  .stat-label {
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    margin-top: 4px;
  }

  .chapter-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr);
    gap: 1px;
    background: var(--light-rule);
    border: 1px solid var(--light-rule);
    margin-top: 2px;
  }
  .chapter-card {
    background: var(--white);
    padding: 22px 20px 18px;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 0.15s;
    position: relative;
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .chapter-card:hover { background: var(--cream); }
  .chapter-card:hover .chapter-arrow { transform: translateX(4px); }
  .chapter-num {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: 48px;
    font-weight: 900;
    color: var(--light-rule);
    line-height: 1;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .chapter-flag {
    font-size: 22px;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .chapter-name {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: 16px;
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .chapter-desc {
    font-size: 12px;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    line-height: 1.5;
    margin-bottom: 12px;
  }
  .chapter-meta {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
  }
  .chapter-count {
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold);
  }
  .chapter-arrow {
    font-size: 16px;
    color: var(--rust);
    transition: transform 0.2s;
  }
  .chapter-card.completed .chapter-num { color: var(--sage); opacity: 0.3; }
  .chapter-badge {
    position: absolute;
    top: 12px;
    right: 12px;
    background: var(--sage);
    color: white;
    font-size: 9px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    padding: 3px 7px;
    border-radius: 2px;
  }

  /* ── QUIZ SCREEN ── */
  #screen-quiz { animation: fadeIn 0.3s ease; display: none; }

  .quiz-header {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--cream);
    padding: 16px 20px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: space-between;
    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--rust);
  }
  .quiz-chapter-name {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 700;
    font-style: italic;
  }
  .quiz-progress-text {
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold);
  }
  .btn-back {
    background: none;
    border: 1px solid var(--warm-gray);
    color: var(--cream);
    padding: 6px 14px;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.1em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif;
    transition: border-color 0.15s;
  }
  .btn-back:hover { border-color: var(--cream); }

  .progress-bar-wrap {
    height: 3px;
    background: rgba(255,255,255,0.1);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .progress-bar-fill {
    height: 100%;
    background: var(--rust);
    transition: width 0.4s ease;
  }

  .quiz-body { padding: 32px 0; }

  .question-kicker {
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.2em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 10px;
  }
  .question-kicker::after { content: ''; flex: 1; height: 1px; background: var(--light-rule); }

  .question-text {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: clamp(20px, 3.5vw, 28px);
    font-weight: 700;
    line-height: 1.3;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
    max-width: 680px;
  }

  .options-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 10px;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  .option-btn {
    background: var(--white);
    border: 1px solid var(--light-rule);
    border-left: 3px solid transparent;
    padding: 16px 18px;
    text-align: left;
    cursor: pointer;
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-size: 14px;
    line-height: 1.4;
    color: var(--ink);
    transition: all 0.15s;
    position: relative;
  }
  .option-btn:hover:not(:disabled) {
    border-left-color: var(--rust);
    background: var(--cream);
  }
  .option-btn.correct {
    background: #EFF5EC;
    border-color: var(--sage);
    border-left-color: var(--sage);
    color: var(--sage);
  }
  .option-btn.wrong {
    background: #FAF0EC;
    border-color: #D4957A;
    border-left-color: var(--rust);
    color: #8B4030;
  }
  .option-btn.reveal {
    background: #EFF5EC;
    border-color: var(--sage);
    border-left-color: var(--sage);
    opacity: 0.5;
  }
  .option-btn:disabled { cursor: default; }
  .option-label {
    font-size: 10px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 4px;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
  }
  .option-btn.correct .option-label { color: var(--sage); }
  .option-btn.wrong .option-label { color: var(--rust); }

  .feedback-box {
    border-top: 2px solid var(--ink);
    padding: 20px 0 0;
    display: none;
    animation: slideUp 0.3s ease;
  }
  .feedback-box.show { display: block; }
  .feedback-result {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: 18px;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .feedback-result.win { color: var(--sage); }
  .feedback-result.lose { color: var(--rust); }
  .feedback-fact {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #4A3F35;
    max-width: 620px;
    margin-bottom: 20px;
    padding-left: 16px;
    border-left: 2px solid var(--gold);
  }
  .btn-next {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--cream);
    border: none;
    padding: 13px 32px;
    font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 0.15s;
  }
  .btn-next:hover { background: var(--rust); }

  /* ── RESULTS SCREEN ── */
  #screen-results { display: none; animation: fadeIn 0.4s ease; }

  .results-masthead {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--cream);
    padding: 40px 28px;
    text-align: center;
    border-bottom: 3px solid var(--rust);
    margin-bottom: 0;
  }
  .results-kicker {
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.25em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--gold);
    margin-bottom: 10px;
  }
  .results-headline {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: clamp(32px, 6vw, 56px);
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin-bottom: 6px;
  }
  .results-headline em { color: var(--rust); font-style: italic; }
  .results-sub {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
  }

  .results-body { padding: 32px 0; }
  .score-card {
    background: var(--white);
    border: 1px solid var(--light-rule);
    border-top: 3px solid var(--ink);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 0;
    margin-bottom: 28px;
  }
  .score-item {
    padding: 24px 20px;
    text-align: center;
    border-right: 1px solid var(--light-rule);
  }
  .score-item:last-child { border-right: none; }
  .score-big {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: 52px;
    font-weight: 900;
    line-height: 1;
    color: var(--rust);
  }
  .score-big.gold { color: var(--gold); }
  .score-big.sage { color: var(--sage); }
  .score-label {
    font-size: 10px;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    color: var(--warm-gray);
    margin-top: 6px;
  }

  .verdict-block {
    padding: 24px 28px;
    background: var(--white);
    border: 1px solid var(--light-rule);
    border-left: 4px solid var(--rust);
    margin-bottom: 24px;
  }
  .verdict-title {
    font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif;
    font-size: 22px;
    font-weight: 700;
    margin-bottom: 8px;
  }
  .verdict-text {
    font-family: 'Libre Baskerville', serif;
    font-size: 14px;
    font-style: italic;
    line-height: 1.7;
    color: #4A3F35;
  }

  .results-actions { display: flex; gap: 12px; flex-wrap: wrap; }
  .btn-primary {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--cream);
    border: none;
    padding: 14px 32px;
    font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: background 0.15s;
  }
  .btn-primary:hover { background: var(--rust); }
  .btn-secondary {
    background: none;
    color: var(--ink);
    border: 1px solid var(--ink);
    padding: 14px 32px;
    font-family: 'DM Sans', sans-serif;
    font-size: 12px;
    font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    cursor: pointer;
    transition: all 0.15s;
  }
  .btn-secondary:hover { background: var(--cream); }

  /* ── SCOREBOARD ── */
  .scoreboard-strip {
    background: var(--ink);
    color: var(--cream);
    padding: 10px 20px;
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    gap: 32px;
    font-size: 11px;
    letter-spacing: 0.15em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
  }
  .score-strip-item { display: flex; align-items: center; gap: 8px; }
  .score-strip-val { color: var(--gold); font-family: 'Playfair Display', serif; font-size: 18px; font-weight: 700; }

  @keyframes fadeIn { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(8px); } to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); } }
  @keyframes slideUp { from { opacity: 0; transform: translateY(12px); } to { opacity: 1; transform: translateY(0); } }

  @media (max-width: 600px) {
    /* Page padding */
    .page { padding: 0 14px 48px; }

    /* Masthead */
    .masthead { padding: 14px 16px 12px; }
    .masthead-kicker { font-size: 9px; }
    .masthead-sub { font-size: 12px; }

    /* Scoreboard */
    .scoreboard-strip { gap: 16px; padding: 8px 12px; font-size: 9px; }
    .score-strip-val { font-size: 15px; }

    /* Intro block */
    .intro-block { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .intro-text { border-right: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--light-rule); padding: 20px 16px; }
    .intro-text h2 { font-size: 22px; }
    .intro-stats { flex-direction: row; justify-content: space-around; padding: 16px; gap: 0; }
    .stat { padding-bottom: 0; border-bottom: none; }
    .stat-num { font-size: 32px; }

    /* Chapter grid */
    .chapter-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .chapter-card { padding: 16px 14px 14px; }
    .chapter-num { font-size: 36px; margin-bottom: 4px; }
    .chapter-name { font-size: 15px; }

    /* Quiz header */
    .quiz-header { padding: 12px 14px; gap: 8px; }
    .quiz-chapter-name { font-size: 14px; }
    .btn-back { padding: 5px 10px; font-size: 10px; }
    .quiz-progress-text { font-size: 10px; white-space: nowrap; }

    /* Questions */
    .question-text {
      font-size: clamp(17px, 4.5vw, 22px);
      margin-bottom: 18px;
    }
    .options-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; gap: 8px; margin-bottom: 18px; }
    .option-btn { padding: 14px 14px; font-size: 14px; }

    /* Feedback */
    .feedback-fact { font-size: 13px; }
    .btn-next { width: 100%; padding: 14px; text-align: center; }

    /* Results */
    .results-masthead { padding: 28px 16px; }
    .score-card { grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr 1fr; }
    .score-big { font-size: 32px; }
    .score-item { padding: 16px 10px; }
    .score-item { border-right: none; border-bottom: 1px solid var(--light-rule); }
    .score-card { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
    .verdict-block { padding: 18px 16px; }
    .results-actions { flex-direction: column; }
    .btn-primary, .btn-secondary { width: 100%; text-align: center; padding: 15px; }

    /* Section label */
    .section-label { margin: 20px 0 14px; }
  }
</style>
</head>
<body>

<!-- MASTHEAD -->
<div class="masthead">
  <div class="masthead-kicker">The Culinary Trivia Gazette</div>
  <div class="masthead-title">Gulp of <span>Knowledge</span></div>
  <div class="masthead-sub">Six chapters. Sixty questions. One table to rule them all.</div>
  <div class="masthead-rule"><span></span><em>✦</em><span></span></div>
</div>

<!-- LIVE SCOREBOARD -->
<div class="scoreboard-strip">
  <div class="score-strip-item"><span>Total Score</span><span class="score-strip-val" id="total-score">0</span></div>
  <div class="score-strip-item"><span>Chapters</span><span class="score-strip-val" id="chapters-done">0/6</span></div>
  <div class="score-strip-item"><span>Streak</span><span class="score-strip-val" id="streak">0</span></div>
</div>

<!-- ══ HOME SCREEN ══ -->
<div id="screen-home">
  <div class="page">
    <div class="intro-block">
      <div class="intro-text">
        <h2>How well do you know <em>what's on your plate?</em></h2>
        <p>Gulp of Knowledge is a culinary trivia journey through six chapters of food history, technique, and culture. Each question comes with a bite of knowledge — because the best answer is always the one that teaches you something.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="intro-stats">
        <div class="stat"><div class="stat-num">6</div><div class="stat-label">Chapters</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="stat-num">60</div><div class="stat-label">Questions</div></div>
        <div class="stat"><div class="stat-num">∞</div><div class="stat-label">Things to learn</div></div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="section-label">Select a Chapter to Begin</div>
    <div class="chapter-grid" id="chapter-grid"></div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ══ QUIZ SCREEN ══ -->
<div id="screen-quiz">
  <div class="quiz-header">
    <button class="btn-back" onclick="goHome()">← Chapters</button>
    <div class="quiz-chapter-name" id="quiz-chapter-title"></div>
    <div class="quiz-progress-text" id="quiz-progress-text"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="progress-bar-wrap">
    <div class="progress-bar-fill" id="progress-bar"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="page">
    <div class="quiz-body">
      <div class="question-kicker" id="question-kicker"></div>
      <div class="question-text" id="question-text"></div>
      <div class="options-grid" id="options-grid"></div>
      <div class="feedback-box" id="feedback-box">
        <div class="feedback-result" id="feedback-result"></div>
        <div class="feedback-fact" id="feedback-fact"></div>
        <button class="btn-next" id="btn-next" onclick="nextQuestion()">Next Question →</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<!-- ══ RESULTS SCREEN ══ -->
<div id="screen-results">
  <div class="results-masthead">
    <div class="results-kicker">Chapter Complete</div>
    <div class="results-headline" id="results-headline"></div>
    <div class="results-sub" id="results-sub"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="page">
    <div class="results-body">
      <div class="score-card">
        <div class="score-item"><div class="score-big" id="res-correct"></div><div class="score-label">Correct</div></div>
        <div class="score-item"><div class="score-big gold" id="res-pct"></div><div class="score-label">Accuracy</div></div>
        <div class="score-item"><div class="score-big sage" id="res-pts"></div><div class="score-label">Points Earned</div></div>
      </div>
      <div class="verdict-block">
        <div class="verdict-title" id="verdict-title"></div>
        <div class="verdict-text" id="verdict-text"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="results-actions">
        <button class="btn-primary" id="btn-retry" onclick="retryChapter()">Retry Chapter</button>
        <button class="btn-secondary" onclick="goHome()">All Chapters</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

<script>
const CHAPTERS = [
  {
    id: 0, flag: '🇮🇹', name: 'Italian Cuisine',
    desc: 'From the hills of Tuscany to the streets of Naples — the art of Italian cooking.',
    color: '#C4522A',
    questions: [
      { q: 'Which Italian region is credited as the birthplace of ragù alla Bolognese?', opts: ['Tuscany', 'Emilia-Romagna', 'Lombardy', 'Veneto'], answer: 1, fact: 'Emilia-Romagna — home of Bologna — is where ragù alla Bolognese originated. The official recipe registered with the Bologna Chamber of Commerce (1982) calls for beef, pancetta, onion, carrot, celery, tomato paste, and milk — no garlic, no herbs.' },
      { q: 'What does "al dente" literally translate to in English?', opts: ['To the bite', 'Just right', 'Firm texture', 'Half cooked'], answer: 0, fact: '"Al dente" means "to the tooth" — pasta cooked so it offers slight resistance when bitten. This preserves a lower glycemic index compared to overcooked pasta, as it slows the digestion of starch.' },
      { q: 'Which Italian cheese is made exclusively from water buffalo milk?', opts: ['Burrata', 'Provolone', 'Mozzarella di Bufala', 'Pecorino'], answer: 2, fact: 'Mozzarella di Bufala Campana holds DOP (Protected Designation of Origin) status. Water buffalo were introduced to Southern Italy by the Normans or Lombards in the medieval period, and the cheese remains concentrated in Campania and Lazio.' },
      { q: 'Risotto achieves its creamy texture primarily through which process?', opts: ['Adding heavy cream', 'Slow addition of stock releasing starch', 'Cooking with butter from the start', 'Using short-grain rice varieties only'], answer: 1, fact: 'The creaminess of risotto comes from slowly coaxing starch out of Arborio or Carnaroli rice through constant agitation and incremental stock additions — a technique called "mantecatura" at the finish, where cold butter is beaten in off the heat.' },
      { q: 'Which Italian preparation literally means "hunter\'s style"?', opts: ['Alla Norma', 'Alla Cacciatora', 'Alla Puttanesca', 'Alla Amatriciana'], answer: 1, fact: '"Alla cacciatora" (hunter\'s style) typically involves braising poultry or rabbit with tomatoes, olives, capers, and wine — ingredients hunters could forage or carry. The name appears across many regions with slight variations.' },
      { q: 'Parmigiano-Reggiano must be aged for a minimum of how many months?', opts: ['12 months', '18 months', '24 months', '36 months'], answer: 0, fact: 'Parmigiano-Reggiano DOP minimum aging is 12 months, but wheels are often sold at 24 (Vecchio) or 36 months (Stravecchio). Inspectors from the Consorzio tap each wheel with a hammer — listening for hollow spots — before applying the fire-branded mark.' },
      { q: 'What is the key difference between Italian and American "pepperoni"?', opts: ['American pepperoni contains more fat', 'Italian salami is rarely called pepperoni — the word means bell pepper', 'Italian pepperoni is always sliced thicker', 'American pepperoni is cured longer'], answer: 1, fact: '"Peperone" in Italian means bell pepper. The spiced pork-and-beef sausage Americans know as pepperoni is an Italian-American creation. Ordering "pizza con peperoni" in Italy will get you a vegetarian pizza with capsicum.' },
      { q: 'Gremolata — the traditional garnish for Osso Buco — consists of which three ingredients?', opts: ['Parsley, lemon zest, garlic', 'Basil, capers, anchovy', 'Mint, orange peel, pine nuts', 'Sage, butter, Parmesan'], answer: 0, fact: 'Gremolata is simply minced lemon zest, garlic, and flat-leaf parsley, scattered over braised veal shanks at the moment of serving. Its brightness cuts through the rich collagen-rich braise and lifts the entire dish.' },
